[18.347658, "o", "\u001b[36mPAY-1\u001b[39m Refund fails for guest orders\r\n\u001b[90mInvestigated /tmp/claude-0/demo/work/pay-api @ f7920ce with dev — Completed\u001b[39m\r\n\r\nPAY-1 reports \"Refund fails for guest orders\". The behaviour lives in the request handling path, where an edge case is not handled.\r\n\r\n\u001b[36m1. Unhandled edge case in the request handler\u001b[39m  \u001b[90m[High]\u001b[39m\r\n   The handler assumes a value that is missing for this case and fails.\r\n   \u001b[90mEvidence:\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[35mREADME.md:1\u001b[39m  Entry point described here.\r\n   \u001b[90mFailing test:\u001b[39m Add a unit test that sends the failing case and expects success.\r\n   \u001b[90mFix:\u001b[39m Guard the missing value and fall back to the default path.\r\n\r\n\u001b[36m2. Stale cached state\u001b[39m  \u001b[90m[Medium]\u001b[39m\r\n   A cached value from an earlier request is reused.\r\n   \u001b[90mEvidence:\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[35mREADME.md\u001b[39m  Caching mentioned in the overview.\r\n   \u001b[90mFailing test:\u001b[39m Add a test that runs two requests in a row.\r\n   \u001b[90mFix:\u001b[39m Key the cache by the request owner.\r\n\r\nHypothesis 1 is being fixed by feature eeb78213-5ef8-4211-a9c5-542c26ce0d3d.\r\n"]
